menu "Daily Mirror application"

config MIRROR_FW_VERSION
    string "Firmware version reported in mDNS and /stats"
    default "0.1.0"

config MIRROR_STA_TIMEOUT_S
    int "Seconds to wait for a station address before starting the setup network"
    default 60
    range 10 600
    help
        The station keeps trying forever in the background either way; this is
        only how long the device waits before *also* offering the fallback
        access point, so someone can reach /config and fix the credentials.

config MIRROR_AP_PASSWORD
    string "WPA2 password for the fallback setup network"
    default "dailymirror"
    help
        The setup access point is named after the mDNS hostname
        (mirror-<last 3 MAC bytes>) and carries the same admin server, so
        /config is reachable on a device that has never joined a network.

        Eight characters or more, or the network comes up open. This is a
        build-time default for bench units and is documented in
        firmware/README.md - it is not a secret, and a shipping product should
        derive a per-device password instead.

config MIRROR_DEBUG_ISP_STATS
    bool "Log the ISP 3A statistics at debug level"
    default n
    help
        Turns esp_ipa and esp_video up to DEBUG at start-up: every
        auto-exposure decision, white-balance gain and autofocus score. This is
        how the IMX519's focus band and the purple-blacks pedestal were found,
        so it stays available - but it is far too noisy to leave on, and on the
        ESP32-S3 (which has no ISP) it does nothing.

        See also CAMERA_IMX519_DEBUG_LOG under "Camera Sensor (IMX add-on)",
        which logs the sensor-side exposure and gain writes.

endmenu
